# Sidebar

Expects only two child elements

## Usage

```html
<div class="l-sidebar">
	<div>Sidebar</div>
	<div>Main content</div>
</div>
```

## Default

<SqueezeContainer>
	<div class="l-sidebar">
		<div class="sidebar__content">Sidebar</div>
		<div class="sidebar__main-content">Main content</div>
	</div>
</SqueezeContainer>

## Custom properties

| Property name            | Default value |
| ------------------------ | ------------- |
| `--sidebar-content-min-width--component` | `75%`         |
| `--sidebar-space--component` | `var(--s-1)`  |
| `--sidebar-width--component` | `initial`     |

## Exception class

`e-sidebar-on-right` - when the sidebar is on the right side of the screen

<PropBoolean name="sidebarOnRight" bind:value={sidebarOnRight} />
<PropSelect
	options={percent_options}
	name="sidebarContentMinWidth"
	bind:value={sidebarContentMinWidth}
/>
<PropSelect options={space_options} name="sidebarSpace" bind:value={sidebarSpace} />
<PropSelect options={measure_options} name="sidebarWidth" bind:value={sidebarWidth} />

<SqueezeContainer>
	<div 
		style="--sidebar-content-min-width--component: {sidebarContentMinWidth}; --sidebar-space--component: {sidebarSpace}; --sidebar-width--component: {sidebarWidth};"
		class="l-sidebar {sidebarOnRight ? 'e-sidebar-on-right' : ''}"
		>
		<div class="sidebar__content">Sidebar</div>
		<div class="sidebar__main-content">Main content</div>
	</div>
</SqueezeContainer>

## Example with content

